00:31:36.630 --> 00:31:41.160
obsolescence risks, momentum
risks, what have you.

00:31:41.160 --> 00:31:45.390
And so I'm very fascinated
to x-ray your mind

00:31:45.390 --> 00:31:47.550
and understand your decision

00:31:47.550 --> 00:31:51.900
around whether now is the
time if you're prepared

00:31:51.900 --> 00:31:54.930
and how you plan to execute that.

00:31:54.930 --> 00:31:55.763
- Yeah.

00:31:57.210 --> 00:32:00.300
I think it's funny because
the rocket launch is correct,

00:32:00.300 --> 00:32:02.670
but I think that people all...

00:32:02.670 --> 00:32:03.900
When you think of rocket
launches, you think

00:32:03.900 --> 00:32:05.580
of SpaceX, right?

00:32:05.580 --> 00:32:07.350
They fired a lot of rockets,

00:32:07.350 --> 00:32:10.203
but they've also blown up a
lot of rockets in general.

00:32:12.821 --> 00:32:15.150
And obviously you shouldn't
take those things lightly,

00:32:15.150 --> 00:32:17.400
but iteration velocity matters a lot

00:32:17.400 --> 00:32:19.290
and being able to set
people up for that kind

00:32:19.290 --> 00:32:21.750
of safe failure matters a lot.

00:32:21.750 --> 00:32:24.120
And of course, there is a marquee flight.

00:32:24.120 --> 00:32:26.160
There is a flight where you
go and you put people on

00:32:26.160 --> 00:32:28.920
that thing and that thing cannot explode.

00:32:28.920 --> 00:32:33.240
And I think that a lot of
the tee up, my dad used

00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:37.740
to say this thing, which is like you work

00:32:37.740 --> 00:32:41.190
for six months before the race
and then you show up, right?

00:32:41.190 --> 00:32:43.361
And most of the work is done before that.

00:32:43.361 --> 00:32:44.194
It's all in preparation.

00:32:44.194 --> 00:32:45.210
It's all in setting up
those other things, right?

00:32:45.210 --> 00:32:47.460
And so you have to
believe that when you want

00:32:47.460 --> 00:32:49.950
to take those deep marquee kind of bets,

00:32:49.950 --> 00:32:52.320
you have to trust your
gut, you have to believe

00:32:52.320 --> 00:32:54.150
that your approach is
correct, you have to believe

00:32:54.150 --> 00:32:56.760
that the rocket is pointing the right way

00:32:56.760 --> 00:32:59.790
because if it's like this,
it's gonna go like this.

00:32:59.790 --> 00:33:00.990
And you have to do a lot of preparation.

00:33:00.990 --> 00:33:03.570
You have to, you know, like
set up a lot of those things.

00:33:03.570 --> 00:33:06.150
And then ultimately at the end of the day,

00:33:06.150 --> 00:33:07.260
you have to trust your gut.

00:33:07.260 --> 00:33:09.480
You have to trust that like
everybody has worked on

00:33:09.480 --> 00:33:12.960
that system with the
most amount of intention,

00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:15.210
with the most amount of
care, with the most amount

00:33:15.210 --> 00:33:17.130
of whatever to make sure that

00:33:17.130 --> 00:33:20.310
that rocket not just
exits the stratosphere,

00:33:20.310 --> 00:33:23.700
not just makes it to
